992e-05, 0.0001767857902450487]], "new_cot": "1. The force exerted on an object can cause it to accelerate, which in turn can change its velocity and distance traveled.\n2. The distance traveled by an object depends on its initial velocity, acceleration, and the time it takes to travel that distance.\n3. The force exerted on an object is related to its acceleration through Newton's second law (F = ma).\n4. If the force exerted on an object increases, its acceleration will also increase, assuming the mass remains constant.\n5. With a higher acceleration, the object will cover more distance in the same amount of time compared to when the force exerted is lower.", "new_cot_probs": [2.503244544982408e-08, 7.171916394099753e-09, 1.6002706937356947e-09, 7.864960934966803e-06], "cot_prob": [-0.8787838816642761], "cot_step_prob": [-0.92242830991745]}}}
